hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1028","1065 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: My father Bashir ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness a gift he had given me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you give all your children the like of this? He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"1029","1066 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: My father set out with me, carrying me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having given me a gift, to witness him to it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given al-Nu'man this slave boy as a gift; bear witness to it. He said: Did you give all your children the like of this? He said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would you like them to be equal toward you in dutifulness? He said: Yes. He said: Then have someone else witness this."
"1030","1067 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"1031","1068 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us. And Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. And the likeness of one who gives a gift then takes it back is like a dog that ate until, when sated, it vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"1032","1069 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father wants to seize my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. The best of what you eat is from your earnings, and the wealth of your children is from your earnings, so eat it with wholesome enjoyment."
